    "title": "New Orleans Saints acquire Broncos' Devaughn Vele to strengthen receivers - NewsBreak",
    "text": "METAIRIE, La. (Louisiana First) — The New Orleans Saints add a missing piece to their offense, a big-bodied wide receiver. The Saints are trading with the Denver Broncos for wide receiver Devaughn Vele, the organization announced Wednesday. The Broncos received a 2026 fourth-round pick and a 2027 seventh-round pick in exchange for Vele. The 6’5, 210-pound receiver brings much-needed size to the Saints’ receiving room. Before adding Vele, the Saints’ tallest receiver was 6’2. The 2024 seventh-round pick appeared in 13 games, making seven starts in his rookie season with Denver, recording 41 catches for 475 yards and three touchdowns. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Louisiana First News.",
